   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "הוּגְרַס בֶּן לֵוִי וְכוּ׳. תַּנְיָא: כְּשֶׁהוּא נוֹתֵן קוֹלוֹ בִּנְעִימָה, מַכְנִיס גּוּדָלוֹ לְתוֹךְ פִּיו, וּמַנִּיחַ אֶצְבָּעוֹ בֵּין הַנִּימִין, עַד שֶׁהָיוּ אֶחָיו הַכֹּהֲנִים נִזְקָרִים בְּבַת רֹאשׁ לַאֲחוֹרֵיהֶם.",
   "en": "§ The mishna related that «Hugras ben Levi» knew a lesson in the art of music and he did not want to teach it to others. «It was taught» in a baraita: «When» Hugras ben Levi «projects his voice in» a sweet «melody,» he «places his thumb into his mouth and places his finger between the strings» of a lyre and sings. This produced a sound «so» sweet «that his brethren the priests were abruptly taken aback.»"
  }
 ],
